# Designer profile gate (every chat)

**Before any reply or other tool call**, `Read` `<workspace root>/designer-profile.local.md`
(next to `AGENTS.md`, never under `harness/`) — never Glob or file search, which skip gitignored files.

| Result | Action |
|--------|--------|
| **File exists** (`Status: ACTIVE` or `SKIPPED`) | **Stop.** Do not run onboarding, MCP gate, profile `AskQuestion`, squad questions, handoff tables, or handoff menu. Use the profile silently. Handle the user's message. |
| **File not found** | **Output the Muse greeting first** (`harness/designer-onboarding/SKILL.md` § The greeting — both plain-text blocks, no preamble) as the literal first content of your response, **before any other tool call** (only the gate-check `Read` above may precede it). Then run the rest of `SKILL.md` per `harness/ORCHESTRATOR.md` §0. **Forbidden:** future-tense narration instead of the greeting ("I'll greet you, then…"); MCP probe or other tools before the greeting text is already in this response. |

**Never** infer "profile missing" from memory, a new chat, or prior turns.
**Never** run onboarding because the user typed a short message (`df`, `hi`).
The filesystem is the only source of truth.

**No narration leak on this `Read` itself.** Found live (2026-07-17): the
gate-check narrated as "Checking your designer profile, then I'll greet
you back" — a stray bit of internal planning leaking into user-facing
text, announcing the *next* step before its own result is known. Either
run this `Read` silently, or, if you narrate it at all, stop at
"Checking your designer profile..." — never a forward-looking clause
("...then I'll greet you back", "...then I'll continue"). What happens
next is decided by this `Read`'s actual result, not pre-announced.
